---
// Placeholder text of a real shape: a buyer replaces the words, not the structure.
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { contact, site } from '../config';
---

<Page
  heading="Privacy"
  lead={`What ${site.name} collects, which is very little, and what happens to it.`}
  updated="10 June 2026"
  title="Privacy"
  description={`The data ${site.name} collects on this site and in the application, and how long it is kept.`}
>
  <p>
    This is sample text for a theme. Replace it with a policy written for your own product and
    checked by someone qualified to check it. The headings below are the ones most jurisdictions
    expect to see.
  </p>

  <h2>The application</h2>
  <p>
    The index and every file it describes stay on your machine. The application makes one outbound
    request, a version check, no more than once every seven days. It sends the version you are
    running and the operating system family, and it receives the number of the latest release.
    Setting <code>updates.check = false</code> in the settings file stops it.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      No analytics script is loaded unless one is configured, and none is configured here. If one is
      turned on, that provider's own terms apply to whatever it collects.
    </li>
    <li>
      No cookies are set. The light and dark preference is kept in local storage on your device.
    </li>
    <li>Web fonts are served from this domain, so no request reaches a font provider.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Purchases</h2>
  <p>
    Payment is handled by a third-party processor, which receives your billing details directly and
    shares with us the email address, the country for tax purposes, and the amount. We keep those
    for as long as tax law requires us to.
  </p>

  <h2>Asking us about your data</h2>
  <p>
    Write to <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>. We will answer within thirty
    days, and sooner in practice.
  </p>
</Page>
